{
  "_comment": [
    "Registry of MANDATORY RECURRING audits (docs/design/ROADMAP.md 'Code health program').",
    "run_all.sh runs the cheap per-commit audits every time; the scans below are too slow,",
    "too network-bound or too human-judgement-heavy for that, so they run on a cadence and",
    "tools/audit/audit_periodic_freshness.py fails the suite once one is overdue.",
    "After running one, stamp it:",
    "  python tools/audit/audit_periodic_freshness.py --record <id> --evidence <path-or-url>",
    "cadence_days = how often it MUST run. grace_days = slack before the suite goes red.",
    "procedure = the full periodic run (the script alone is the per-commit part)."
  ],
  "grace_days": 7,
